# KNOWN GAP — the `float` → `float32` TYPE CHECK is enforced at declared-slot
# and plain-call-arg positions and NOT at CONSUMING positions, and every
# position that escapes it stores zero.
#
# The checker knows this is an error. Measured, `gg check` alone:
#
#     float32 x = 1.5           local bind        -> REJECTED  E_TypeMismatch
#     takes(1.5)                plain call arg    -> REJECTED  E_TypeMismatch
#     Box[float32](1.5)         Box ctor          -> ACCEPTED  prints 0.000000
#     S(1.5)  where S.f:float32 struct ctor       -> ACCEPTED  prints 0.000000
#     v.push(1.5) on Vector[float32]              -> ACCEPTED  prints 0.000000
#
# The rejected spelling and the accepted ones describe the SAME operation:
# putting an `f64` literal into an `f32` slot. Where it is rejected the user
# gets `expected float32, found float`; where it is accepted the value is
# written eight bytes wide into a four-byte slot and reads back as `0.000000`.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE CONSUMING-POSITION SET, on the TYPE axis. It is the same shape
# as the ownership gap already filed for those positions — the rule holds at a
# bare binding and a plain argument, and the constructor / collection-put
# family escapes it — which is why the fix belongs at the shared consuming-arg
# expected-type hint rather than at three sites.
#
# ⛔ DISCRIMINATOR from its neighbour
# `known_gaps/box_float32_element_reads_zero.gg`: THAT one uses an explicit
# `1.5 as float32`, so the source really is `float32` and the checker has
# nothing to say — it fails in the C emitter instead. This one is the CHECKER
# half. Both print `0.000000`, and fixing either alone leaves the other live,
# so a repro that does not state which half it exercises adjudicates neither.
#
# EXPECTED (what the language SHOULD do): `gg check` REJECTS all three
# accepted rows with `E_TypeMismatch`, naming `float32` and `float`, exactly as
# it already does for the local bind and the plain call argument. If instead an
# implicit f64->f32 narrowing at consuming positions is ratified, then all
# three must print 1.500000 — what must NOT stand is accepting them and
# storing zero.
#
# EXPECTED, as asserted by the test that cites this file: `gg check` FAILS.

struct S:
    float32 f

void main():
    Box[float32] a = Box[float32](1.5)
    S s = S(1.5)
    Vector[float32] v = []
    v.push(1.5)
    print((*a))
    print(s.f)
    print(v.get(0).unwrap())
